  "title": "Phosphorus spins in a tumbling Posner stay coherent for about a day",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "29f8a2c2-a659-4101-899f-4f4c2804a921",
      "text": "Rapid tumbling of Posner molecules in water averages the dipole fields of nearby protons to zero, and the residual fluctuations give the phosphorus spins coherence times estimated at about $10^5$ seconds, roughly a day, with a later estimate of 21 days.",
